.TH QSLMANAGERXML 5 "June 2026" "QSLManager 1.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
QSLManagerXML \- QSL Layout XML and Award Definition Specification
.SH SYNOPSIS
A comprehensive XML layout schema specification for defined awards and QSL card layouts (with dynamic goal generation attributes).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B QSLManagerXML
defines the standard XML implementation schema enabling flexible parsing of dynamic awards logic and rendered card formats across AdifMonitor instances.
.PP
The schema handles validation and generation of:
.IP \[bu] 3
QSL card rendering measurements and layouts (positions, fonts, checklists).
.IP \[bu]
Award Tracking Metadata directly coupling logical goals to presentation layers.
.IP \[bu]
QSO Log Structure parsing definitions.
.SH FORMAT STRUCTURE
The primary node is 
.B <QSLLayout>
with attributes denoting formatting rules (e.g. \fBdateFormat\fP, \fBtimeFormat\fP).
.PP
.B Checkboxes
and
.B Fields
derive physical coordinate boundaries on printed definitions while actively hooking onto dynamically populated attributes parsing straight from defined goals within the SQLite and JSON configurations.
.SH AWARD CRITERIA BINDINGS
The XML integrates natively with award tracking rules using the 
.B <AwardCriteria> 
block. This node optionally hosts \fBawardName\fP, \fBAuthor\fP, and localized plain English \fBCriteriaDescription\fP tags, along with nested generic \fBCriteriaRule\fP string arrays bridging AdifMonitor criteria checks into portable definitions.
.SH VALIDATION
Compliant documents validate successfully against \fBqsl_layout.xsd\fP ensuring data safety.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBadifmanager\fP(1)
